{#
  Jonson CTA beat — the ways-to-connect moment inside a response ([[contact]]).

  ONE BUTTON, for everyone, VIP or not. Its label is fixed — "Let’s talk more" —
  because it follows a reply that has just made the case, so it continues the
  conversation rather than asking the contact single’s question again (that copy
  stays on the contact page and panel).

  The other routes a VIP’s door opens — call, WhatsApp — are NOT buttons here. They
  belong in the sentence, written as links by the model and rendered by
  inlineMarkdown() in jonson-ask.js against the allowlist the page carries
  (data-jonson-links, set on .c-jonson in _views/single/home). A row of buttons in the
  middle of a conversation reads as a form; "call me on <number>" reads as a person
  saying it. The contact page and the footer are where a row of buttons belongs.

  Expects: contact — the contact single entry.
#}
{% if contact is defined and contact %}
    <div class="c-ctas c-ctas--jonson">
        {% include '_components/button.twig' with {
            label: 'Let’s talk more',
            href:  siteUrl('contact'),
            size:  'md',
        } only %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
